{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured persistent rsyslog forwarding of `inventory` messages from node2 to node1 over TCP/601. Messages are stored at `/var/log/inventory/node2.log`. Verified operation before restart and after sequential restarts of both nodes, without changing the installed RHEL release or kernel.","actions_performed":["Configured node1 as an inventory-only rsyslog collector bound to 10.100.129.10:601.","Persistently opened TCP/601 in node1's firewall.","Configured node2 with persistent TCP forwarding, infinite retry, and a disk-assisted queue.","Verified non-inventory messages are excluded from the destination file.","Safely restarted node1 and node2 one at a time and verified changed boot identities and full recovery."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Forward inventory logs from node2 and persist them on node1 at /var/log/inventory/node2.log","command_ids":["cmd-f5a7a6ab9b6a4312","cmd-4341e39be2a5468d","cmd-f7f6242d93ea4449","cmd-4b7dd905a6964452","cmd-97acf0c392694ed2"],"summary":"The collector listener and firewall are persistent, node2 has an established forwarding connection, and all three inventory test markers were found in the requested file. A non-inventory marker was confirmed absent."},{"requirement":"Keep log flow working after node1 restarts","command_ids":["cmd-355f861b523d4393","cmd-671089514df54fa7","cmd-e8bd7d76f9c14173","cmd-3e8d1d72c7ec4eec","cmd-af079572018946e4"],"summary":"Node1 changed boot ID from 254597f8-4ac9-4062-8be8-44eba1f6d2e9 to 368be977-f84d-4759-a6e0-eca54d06aad8. Its listener, firewall, service, configuration, and existing data recovered, and a new inventory message arrived afterward."},{"requirement":"Keep log flow working after node2 restarts","command_ids":["cmd-d9229c6418014c2a","cmd-14286158ecc74eec","cmd-dfefa6b7fc3042f7","cmd-eb309ce433b549b4","cmd-97acf0c392694ed2"],"summary":"Node2 changed boot ID from 434803ac-a01f-4272-ba59-a0cdb0c4dd92 to e27ea4c9-db0a-4b87-a894-b691d587e1a9. Rsyslog and its forwarding connection recovered, and node1 persisted a new post-restart inventory message."},{"requirement":"Preserve the installed operating-system release and kernel","command_ids":["cmd-e5a7ecaae5aa4100","cmd-b31ecd1a3d2a40aa","cmd-97acf0c392694ed2","cmd-ec22abecde4a4fc7"],"summary":"Both nodes remained on Red Hat Enterprise Linux 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64; the existing RHEL-compatible rsyslog package was used."}]}
